The characterization workflow and motor models are inspired by WPILib SysId.
guanid is an independent PROS/VEX implementation, not a WPILib product, port,
or supported fork. No WPILib or PROS implementation is bundled in its template.
PROS, VEX, WPILib, and other names belong to their respective owners.

Robot projects supply PROS and any other dependencies under their own licenses.
The optional legacy Python analyzer requires NumPy (and matplotlib for PNGs);
those packages are not bundled. The primary C++ library/analyzer needs neither.
